      "requirement": "All applicable engines on U.S.-flagged vessels when operating as OCS source(s), and otherwise not subject to Section IV(C)(2)-(5), shall be certified to the highest applicable EPA Tier Marine Engine Standards (i.e., Tier 3 or 4, depending on engine size) as contained within 40 C.F.R. Part 1042, except if one of the conditions in subparagraph (6)(i) or (6)(ii) is met, in which case the Permittee may use the next lower Tier engine.",
      "scope": "All applicable engines on U.S.-flagged vessels operating as OCS sources",
      "numerical_value": null,
      "unit": null,
      "source": "40 C.F.R. Part 1042",
      "related_domains": ["air emissions", "marine vessel compliance", "environmental impact assessment"]
    },
    {
      "type": "Technical",
      "requirement": "To use a lesser Tier engine, the Permittee shall ensure one of the following conditions is met: i. A vessel with a higher Tier engine is not available within two hours of when the vessel must be deployed; or ii. The total emissions associated with the use of a vessel with the higher Tier engine(s) would be greater than the total emissions associated with the use of the vessel with the next lower Tier engine(s). For purposes of this subparagraph, when determining the total emissions associated with the use of a vessel with a particular engine, the Permittee shall include the emissions of the vessel that would occur when the vessel would be in transit to the WDA from the vessel’s starting location.",
      "scope": "All applicable engines on vessels used for the project when operating as OCS sources",
      "numerical_value": 2,
      "unit": "hours",
      "source": "Revolution Wind, LLC Outer Continental Shelf Preconstruction Air Permit No. OCS-R1-05 Section IV(C)(5) and (6)",
      "related_domains": ["air emissions", "marine vessel compliance", "environmental impact assessment", "logistics"]
    }
